# Architecture

## What This Is
A company operating system for teams. Manage brand voice, generate content, coordinate team workflows — all in one dashboard. Employees log in and see their company workspace.

## Who Uses This
- Employees: access company brand context, generate content, view outputs
- Admins/founders: manage team, configure brand, review all outputs
- External consumers (hub-os): read-only API access to company data (see `external-api.mdc`)

## Stack
- **Frontend + API:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Database + Auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL, RLS enforced)
- **AI:** Anthropic Claude via API routes only — never called from client
- **Deploy:** Vercel
- **Language:** TypeScript strict throughout

## Folder Structure
```
app/
  (auth)/login/          ← auth pages
  (dashboard)/           ← all authenticated pages
    layout.tsx           ← sidebar shell
    page.tsx             ← dashboard home
  api/                   ← all API routes (AI calls live here)
    external/            ← read-only endpoints for external consumers
lib/
  supabase/
    client.ts            ← browser client
    server.ts            ← server client for API routes
  ai/
    prompts.ts           ← ALL prompts live here, nowhere else
    generate.ts          ← AI call logic
  queries/               ← typed database query functions
  schemas/               ← shared Zod schemas
  types/
    database.ts          ← generated from Supabase schema
components/              ← shared UI components
supabase/migrations/     ← schema as code, never touch DB directly
```

## Multi-Tenant
All data is isolated by `organization_id`. Users only see organizations they are members of. See `database.mdc` for query rules and `data-isolation.mdc` for the zero-tolerance security rules.

## Reusability
This codebase is a generic company OS product. All identity (company names, brand content) lives in the database, never in code. Deploying for a new company requires zero code changes — just a fresh Supabase and Vercel deployment. See `template-ready.mdc` for the hard rules.

## External API
This system exposes a read-only external API for trusted consumers like hub-os. See `external-api.mdc` for the rules. This API is authenticated by API key, not user session, and only serves read operations.
